The decision itself
Resolve() is static and reads nothing from the terminal. The function takes the five raw caps and the volume settings. The function returns the status, the volume, and the cap that won. On a tie the cap listed first wins, so RISK is reported rather than OPEN_RISK when both allow the same volume.
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| Resolve: the smallest cap, rounded down to the step. On a tie    |
//| the cap listed first in ENUM_RB_CAP is reported                  |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
