ExposureRisk() makes one OrderCalcProfit() call for the full volume, from the open price to the stop. The same slippage buffer is applied. A position has paid its entry commission, so the function adds the commission of the exit side only. A pending order has not paid it, so both sides are added. The commission is added before the result is clamped at 0. A stop at breakeven, or slightly in profit, therefore still carries the commission that is left to pay. When OrderCalcProfit() fails, the function returns false and does not report a loss of 0. OpenRisk() then counts the position in unpriced, and Quote() refuses the quote.
