The quote
Quote() runs the checks in the order of Figure 1. The margin cap needs an additional check at the end. The margin for 1 lot times the volume is only an estimate, because I don't assume that the margin grows exactly in line with the volume on each symbol. After the final volume is chosen, Quote() calls OrderCalcMargin() again for that exact volume. If the result is still over the allowed margin, the volume is scaled down once and checked again. The trade is refused when that second check fails too.
