On EURUSD the risk per lot goes from 560 to 577 USD. The difference is 7 USD of commission for both sides plus 10 ticks of 1 USD. The stocks show a problem with my own input. A commission per lot is a commission per share on a stock, so 3.5 USD per share adds 7 USD to the risk of each share. INTC, NVDA, and NVT then move from the MARGIN cap to the RISK cap. The 3.5 USD was chosen for forex and is far too high for a share. The input does not know which kind of symbol it is used on. If an EA trades stocks and forex together, it needs a commission per symbol.
Seven symbols in the Strategy Tester
RiskBudgetEA.mq5 is a test driver and has no trading edge. Once a day per symbol, from 10:00 server time on, it opens a position in the direction of the last H1 close against a 50-period moving average. The stop is 0.5% of the price away and the take profit twice that. Stocks wait for their session. When the spread is wider than a fifth of the stop, the EA waits for a later tick.
I added the wait after a run without it (InpMaxSpread=100). In that run the EA sent 56 orders on NVT, and the tester refused 40 of those orders with Invalid stops. In each of the 40 refused orders the spread at the moment of the order was wider than the stop distance. In each of the 16 accepted orders it was narrower. The median spread of the 40 refused orders was 4.31 USD, against a stop distance of about 0.80 USD. The order of the symbols moves by one every day, because the budget goes to whichever symbol asks first.
