On the CFDs and forex pairs the median realized loss was within 2% of the plan. Three stops went further, during fast moves. NVT is different. Its median stop cost 11.5% more than planned, and 18 of 31 stops were more than 10% over. In the tester, NVT stops filled at the next trade price. On NVT that price was often a few cents past the stop. The 5.76 was a sell of 16 shares at 151.03, opened at 2026.09.17 22:43 with the stop at 151.79. The stop filled at the next session open, at 155.41. The stop didn't limit that loss. The budget couldn't limit it either, because the budget is calculated from the stop distances.
